    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37099" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξελεύθερ-ος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>freedman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				197
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				6.5.1
			</span></i>: fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1907
				</span></i>
			.—The special application of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.</span> to a <i>released</i> debtor (cf. Ammon.<i><span class="en">
				p.23
			</span></i> V., <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1751.2
			</span></i>) is not confirmed by usage; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπελεύθερος</span>
			are used of the same person by <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				39.38
			</span></i>.</div>
